WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.960 --> 00:00:02.160
Have you ever wondered

00:00:02.160 --> 00:00:06.080
if there are more natural ways
to lower your high blood pressure,

00:00:06.080 --> 00:00:09.040
guard against Alzheimer's,
lose weight, and feel better?

00:00:09.040 --> 00:00:12.240
Well, it turns out there is!

00:00:12.240 --> 00:00:14.720
Welcome to the
Nutrition Facts Podcast.

00:00:14.720 --> 00:00:18.560
I’m your host,
Dr. Michael Greger.

00:00:18.560 --> 00:00:20.240
Today we look at the
body of evidence

00:00:20.240 --> 00:00:24.160
that links pesticides to
serious health problems.
 &nbsp;

00:00:24.160 --> 00:00:28.880
And we start with an episode guest
hosted by Dr. Kristine Dennis,

00:00:28.880 --> 00:00:31.280
our new Senior Research Scientist,

00:00:31.280 --> 00:00:34.080
who has been researching and
scripting new video topics.

00:00:34.080 --> 00:00:38.800
In this video, Kristine delves into
the association of vegetarian diets

00:00:38.800 --> 00:00:41.440
and hypospadias birth defects

00:00:41.440 --> 00:00:44.880
to see if it holds up in
the light of new research.

00:00:44.880 --> 00:00:48.800
In 2000, a study found that a
vegetarian diet during pregnancy

00:00:48.800 --> 00:00:51.200
was associated with hypospadias,

00:00:51.200 --> 00:00:53.840
a specific birth defect
of the penis.

00:00:53.840 --> 00:00:55.840
The authors suggested
that it may be due

00:00:55.840 --> 00:00:58.240
to the greater exposure
to phytoestrogens,

00:00:58.240 --> 00:01:00.480
which are found in soy foods.

00:01:00.480 --> 00:01:02.000
But if you look globally,

00:01:02.000 --> 00:01:03.520
while there is
an extraordinarily

00:01:03.520 --> 00:01:06.320
high prevalence
in North America and Europe,

00:01:06.320 --> 00:01:09.920
it's extremely low
in a country like Japan,

00:01:09.920 --> 00:01:13.600
which has the highest per capita
soy intake in the world.

00:01:13.600 --> 00:01:14.880
In fact, in Japan,

00:01:14.880 --> 00:01:17.680
a low maternal intake
of soy phytoestrogens

00:01:17.680 --> 00:01:21.200
has been associated with
elevated risk of hypospadias,

00:01:21.200 --> 00:01:25.120
so, if anything,
soy may be protective.

00:01:25.120 --> 00:01:27.600
If soy foods aren't
the hormone disrupters,

00:01:27.600 --> 00:01:30.160
what in a vegetarian diet
might be?

00:01:30.160 --> 00:01:32.480
Well, occupational
exposure to pesticides

00:01:32.480 --> 00:01:34.960
is associated with higher risk,

00:01:34.960 --> 00:01:38.160
so, might low-level pesticide
exposure among those eating

00:01:38.160 --> 00:01:40.800
more fruits and vegetables--
like vegetarians--

00:01:40.800 --> 00:01:42.960
help explain it?

00:01:42.960 --> 00:01:44.240
If you randomize people

00:01:44.240 --> 00:01:46.960
to a more plant-based
Mediterranean diet,

00:01:46.960 --> 00:01:49.440
you see a large increase
in the amount of pesticides

00:01:49.440 --> 00:01:51.440
flowing through their body,
though, of course,

00:01:51.440 --> 00:01:53.360
if you put them
on a Mediterranean diet

00:01:53.360 --> 00:01:55.440
with organic fruits
and vegetables,

00:01:55.440 --> 00:01:59.840
you see a 90 percent drop
in pesticide exposure.

00:01:59.840 --> 00:02:02.800
So, does organic food
consumption during pregnancy

00:02:02.800 --> 00:02:05.200
reduce hypospadias risk?

00:02:05.200 --> 00:02:09.040
Apparently so,
cutting the odds about in half,

00:02:09.040 --> 00:02:10.720
particularly when
it comes to choosing

00:02:10.720 --> 00:02:12.880
organic vegetables and dairy,

00:02:12.880 --> 00:02:14.000
though the only other study

00:02:14.000 --> 00:02:16.560
to look at organic food choices
and hypospadias

00:02:16.560 --> 00:02:17.920
found the risk associated

00:02:17.920 --> 00:02:21.600
just with conventional
high-fat dairy products.

00:02:21.600 --> 00:02:23.200
It isn't all or nothing.

00:02:23.200 --> 00:02:26.080
Even if only two thirds
of your produce is organic,

00:02:26.080 --> 00:02:29.280
that can significantly reduce
pesticide exposure,

00:02:29.280 --> 00:02:32.320
but the benefits of consuming
conventionally grown produce

00:02:32.320 --> 00:02:36.560
likely outweigh any possible
risks from pesticide exposure,

00:02:36.560 --> 00:02:38.720
so, concerns over
ingesting pesticides

00:02:38.720 --> 00:02:41.920
should never discourage
fruit and vegetable intake.

00:02:41.920 --> 00:02:43.360
In the United States alone,

00:02:43.360 --> 00:02:46.080
if you add up all
of the fatal cancers, strokes,

00:02:46.080 --> 00:02:48.880
heart attacks, and other deaths
that could have been averted

00:02:48.880 --> 00:02:51.520
simply by eating
more fruits and vegetables,

00:02:51.520 --> 00:02:56.400
it comes out to nearly
450,000 deaths every year.

00:02:56.400 --> 00:02:58.880
That's how powerful
produce can be.

00:02:58.880 --> 00:03:03.520
But might one of the downsides
be this hypospadias risk?

00:03:03.520 --> 00:03:05.520
Despite their high
plant consumption,

00:03:05.520 --> 00:03:09.360
vegetarians may be less exposed
to conventional pesticides,

00:03:09.360 --> 00:03:11.280
but that's because
of their greater propensity

00:03:11.280 --> 00:03:13.840
to choose organic produce.

00:03:13.840 --> 00:03:16.160
Now, the researchers only
considered the pesticides

00:03:16.160 --> 00:03:18.640
in plant foods,
not animal products,

00:03:18.640 --> 00:03:20.880
and even for
conventional insecticides,

00:03:20.880 --> 00:03:23.840
animal products are
main contributors to exposure.

00:03:24.400 --> 00:03:26.560
Additionally,
persistent pesticides,

00:03:26.560 --> 00:03:29.920
such as organochlorine
pesticides like DDT,

00:03:29.920 --> 00:03:33.520
are concentrated in fish,
other meats, and dairy,

00:03:33.520 --> 00:03:34.480
so it's no surprise

00:03:34.480 --> 00:03:36.480
that the blood of
strictly plant-based eaters

00:03:36.480 --> 00:03:39.520
ends up significantly
less polluted.

00:03:39.520 --> 00:03:43.440
It may not just be from the
lower level of intake, though;

00:03:43.440 --> 00:03:47.680
high fiber diets can bulk up the
stool and glom on to pesticides

00:03:47.680 --> 00:03:50.400
and flush them away.

00:03:50.400 --> 00:03:53.280
In the end, the hypospadias
issue may be another example

00:03:53.280 --> 00:03:54.800
of the stroke scare.

00:03:54.800 --> 00:03:57.920
Dr. Greger did a whole series
covering potential explanations

00:03:57.920 --> 00:04:01.840
why a study had found higher
stroke rates among vegetarians,

00:04:01.840 --> 00:04:04.720
but then, half a dozen
other studies found

00:04:04.720 --> 00:04:09.120
lower rates of stroke,
if anything, across the board.

00:04:09.120 --> 00:04:12.960
The original hypospadias study
looked at about 50 cases.

00:04:12.960 --> 00:04:13.840
Twelve years later,

00:04:13.840 --> 00:04:18.080
a study that looked
at 1,250 cases was published

00:04:18.080 --> 00:04:22.480
and found zero increased risk
among vegetarian mothers.

00:04:22.480 --> 00:04:23.440
In our next story,

00:04:23.440 --> 00:04:25.680
researchers measure the
impact of eating organic

00:04:25.680 --> 00:04:28.640
on the levels of
pesticides in our children.

00:04:28.640 --> 00:04:31.600
Produce can be contaminated
by manure runoff,

00:04:31.600 --> 00:04:36.720
and conventional produce may
be contaminated with pesticides.

00:04:36.720 --> 00:04:40.480
We’ve known for years
that the 800 million pounds

00:04:40.480 --> 00:04:43.360
of pesticides used annually
in the United States—

00:04:44.160 --> 00:04:47.360
herbicides, fungicides, insecticides—

00:04:47.360 --> 00:04:51.440
have clear-cut detrimental effects
on farm workers and their families.

00:04:51.440 --> 00:04:53.200
That’s uncontroversial.

00:04:53.200 --> 00:04:56.160
We can even do what are
called hand-wipe studies

00:04:56.160 --> 00:04:58.480
to actually measure the pesticides

00:04:58.480 --> 00:05:01.680
in the hands of kids in
California’s Central Valley.

00:05:02.480 --> 00:05:05.680
The planes come down and spray this fog.

00:05:06.480 --> 00:05:13.040
How much exposure urban and suburban
children are getting from food, however,

00:05:13.040 --> 00:05:15.120
has been unclear,

00:05:15.120 --> 00:05:17.760
until now.

00:05:17.760 --> 00:05:19.920
Twice daily, urine samples were taken

00:05:19.920 --> 00:05:23.760
from 3-to 11-year-olds
for more than a year

00:05:23.760 --> 00:05:29.360
to see how much pesticide
is flowing through our kids.

00:05:29.360 --> 00:05:34.320
These children were nowhere near
farms, or fog-spraying planes.

00:05:34.320 --> 00:05:38.400
And to single out pesticides
that were coming from the diet,

00:05:38.400 --> 00:05:41.440
as opposed to a lawn
treatment or something,

00:05:41.440 --> 00:05:48.000
for two weeks of the year, the
kids were put on organic diet.

00:05:48.000 --> 00:05:51.600
Guess which two weeks those were?

00:05:51.600 --> 00:05:57.360
So the two times during the year
when they ate organic foods,

00:05:57.360 --> 00:06:00.320
there were undetectable,
or nearly undetectable,

00:06:00.320 --> 00:06:03.280
pesticide residues in their urine,

00:06:03.280 --> 00:06:09.200
while their little bodies were basically
swimming in it the rest of the year.

00:06:09.200 --> 00:06:14.480
In my 2000 update, I told everyone
about this disturbing study.

00:06:14.480 --> 00:06:19.120
Vegetarianism during pregnancy
associated with having sons

00:06:19.120 --> 00:06:23.920
with a specific birth defect of
the penis called hypospadias.

00:06:24.480 --> 00:06:29.040
They thought it might have something
to do with the phytoestrogens in soy,

00:06:29.040 --> 00:06:32.560
but that didn’t make
any sense since Japan,

00:06:32.560 --> 00:06:37.120
with the highest per capita
soy consumption in the world,

00:06:37.120 --> 00:06:40.880
did not have high rates of the defect.

00:06:40.880 --> 00:06:46.560
I guessed that it might be low vitamin
B12 levels leading to high homocysteine,

00:06:46.560 --> 00:06:49.600
which has been related
to other birth defects,

00:06:49.600 --> 00:06:53.120
but we were all wrong.

00:06:53.120 --> 00:06:57.280
Finally, though, the mystery
seems to have been solved.

00:06:57.280 --> 00:07:02.960
The researchers reanalyzed the data
for clues as to what could be found

00:07:02.960 --> 00:07:06.640
in the diets of vegetarians
compared to meat eaters—

00:07:06.640 --> 00:07:10.640
other than more good things,
like more fruits and vegetables.

00:07:10.640 --> 00:07:16.640
Unless, there is an endocrine-disrupting
fungicide, called vinclozolin,

00:07:16.640 --> 00:07:20.240
that is sprayed on most
of our conventional crops,

00:07:20.240 --> 00:07:22.640
which we now know causes hypospadias.

00:07:22.640 --> 00:07:27.680
So, researchers went back and split up
the vegetarian moms into two groups:

00:07:27.680 --> 00:07:33.440
those eating organic produce, and
those eating conventional produce.

00:07:33.440 --> 00:07:36.720
And while the vegetarian women
eating conventional produce

00:07:36.720 --> 00:07:41.280
during pregnancy had indeed
higher birth defects rates,

00:07:41.280 --> 00:07:45.920
there was not a single
case in the organic group.

00:07:45.920 --> 00:07:49.920
So it seems the hypospadias
wasn’t due to vegetarian diets;

00:07:49.920 --> 00:07:56.000
it was that they were exposing
their fetus to more pesticides.

00:07:56.000 --> 00:07:59.680
Can’t we just rinse our produce off?

00:07:59.680 --> 00:08:02.160
Well, it’s better than nothing,

00:08:02.160 --> 00:08:07.360
but this new study looked at
three pesticides on apples.

00:08:07.360 --> 00:08:10.080
Levels start out at 100%.

00:08:10.080 --> 00:08:15.600
Rinsing seems to take off only
about 15% of the pesticides.

00:08:15.600 --> 00:08:20.240
The only way to really cut down
our dose is to peel the apple,

00:08:20.240 --> 00:08:23.040
eliminating about 85% of the pesticides—

00:08:23.040 --> 00:08:27.600
but also eliminating
much of the nutrition.

00:08:27.600 --> 00:08:32.480
So, eat organic foods whenever possible.

00:08:32.480 --> 00:08:37.760
Organic produce has more
vitamins, more minerals,

00:08:37.760 --> 00:08:40.160
tastes better, stores better,

00:08:40.160 --> 00:08:48.240
and you get to not be complicit in the
poisoning farm workers and their families.

00:08:48.240 --> 00:08:49.120
Finally today,

00:08:49.120 --> 00:08:51.680
how can we avoid the
breakdown product of pesticides

00:08:51.680 --> 00:08:54.880
that may increase the risk
of Alzheimer’s disease?

00:08:55.440 --> 00:08:57.920
Although there is a growing list
of Alzheimer's disease

00:08:57.920 --> 00:09:00.880
susceptibility genes, even if
you put them all altogether,

00:09:00.880 --> 00:09:04.400
they account for less than half
of all Alzheimer's cases.

00:09:04.400 --> 00:09:07.360
The single most compelling piece
of data on the potential control

00:09:07.360 --> 00:09:10.160
we have over the disease
is the fact that if you have

00:09:10.160 --> 00:09:13.360
identical twins, with the exact
same genes, even if one gets

00:09:13.360 --> 00:09:16.320
Alzheimer's the other
usually does not.

00:09:16.320 --> 00:09:17.920
So, we have to think
about all the other

00:09:17.920 --> 00:09:20.960
contributing factors
beyond just genetics.

00:09:21.680 --> 00:09:25.360
In my video on pesticides and cancer,
I talked about this study.

00:09:25.360 --> 00:09:28.680
There’s a list of chlorinated
pesticides, including DDE

00:09:28.680 --> 00:09:32.480
(a metabolite of DDT) that
are classified by the EPA

00:09:32.480 --> 00:09:34.800
as probable human carcinogens.

00:09:34.800 --> 00:09:37.760
But in the study, blood
levels of DDE and others were

00:09:37.760 --> 00:09:40.720
associated not with
increased cancer mortality,

00:09:40.720 --> 00:09:43.920
but increased risk of
other-cause mortality.

00:09:43.920 --> 00:09:46.240
This led researchers to
speculate it may be due to

00:09:46.240 --> 00:09:50.560
an associated increased risk
of diabetes or dementia.

00:09:50.560 --> 00:09:53.280
I’ve talked previously
about the diabetes link.

00:09:53.280 --> 00:09:55.360
What about dementia?

00:09:55.360 --> 00:10:00.480
“Elevated Serum Pesticide Levels
and Risk for Alzheimer Disease.”

00:10:00.480 --> 00:10:03.840
A research team at Rutgers found
significantly higher blood

00:10:03.840 --> 00:10:08.240
levels of DDE in Alzheimer’s disease
patients compared to controls,

00:10:08.240 --> 00:10:10.080
and autopsy studies
show blood levels

00:10:10.080 --> 00:10:12.960
are a good proxy for brain levels.

00:10:12.960 --> 00:10:15.200
Those with the highest levels
were at about four times

00:10:15.200 --> 00:10:17.680
the odds of being
demented with Alzheimer's.

00:10:17.680 --> 00:10:21.360
And in a petri dish, DDE increases
amyloid precursor protein levels

00:10:21.360 --> 00:10:25.063
in human brain cells, providing
a potential mechanism.

00:10:25.280 --> 00:10:28.000
Put all these studies together,
and there does indeed seem

00:10:28.000 --> 00:10:30.960
to be a link, consistent with
data showing about a doubling

00:10:30.960 --> 00:10:32.640
of risk for developing dementia among

00:10:32.640 --> 00:10:35.440
those acutely pesticide poisoned.

00:10:35.440 --> 00:10:39.360
Among U.S. elders, DDT and its
breakdown product DDE are also

00:10:39.360 --> 00:10:43.440
associated with increased risk
of cognitive decline in general.

00:10:43.440 --> 00:10:46.000
DDT was extensively
used in the United States

00:10:46.000 --> 00:10:47.920
from the 1940s through the 1960s.

00:10:47.920 --> 00:10:52.240
At its peak, we were churning
out 180 million pounds a year.

00:10:52.240 --> 00:10:54.880
And it’s still in our bodies to this day,

00:10:54.880 --> 00:10:58.240
contaminating the bloodstreams of
more than 90 percent of Americans,

00:10:58.240 --> 00:11:01.280
and DDE, the pesticide
linked to quadrupling the odds

00:11:01.280 --> 00:11:03.920
of Alzheimer’s, were at the highest levels.

00:11:03.920 --> 00:11:07.120
It’s still in our bodies because
it’s still in the food supply.

00:11:07.120 --> 00:11:10.000
In my last video on the topic,
I noted that the levels of

00:11:10.000 --> 00:11:13.120
DDT, DDE, and other banned
pesticides and pollutants

00:11:13.120 --> 00:11:16.400
were much lower in the breast
milk from a vegetarian mother

00:11:16.400 --> 00:11:19.520
compared to breast milk of
her non-vegetarian sister.

00:11:19.520 --> 00:11:22.080
And the largest difference
was noted for DDE,

00:11:22.080 --> 00:11:25.600
which was four times lower
in the vegetarian sister.

00:11:25.600 --> 00:11:29.600
This is what you see across the
board for these kinds of pollutants.

00:11:29.600 --> 00:11:32.720
Food samples were collected from
supermarkets across the U.S.

00:11:32.720 --> 00:11:35.040
Here’s what they found
for dioxins and PCBs

00:11:35.040 --> 00:11:39.600
in beef, chicken, pork,
processed meat, eggs, fish,

00:11:39.600 --> 00:11:42.720
all plant-foods put together,
and dairy products.

00:11:42.720 --> 00:11:45.840
These toxins build up the food
chain; so, it makes sense that

00:11:45.840 --> 00:11:50.320
the most contaminated foods are
meat, fish, and dairy products.

00:11:50.320 --> 00:11:53.840
5 to 10 times higher
levels in meat, eggs,

00:11:53.840 --> 00:11:57.440
fish, and dairy than what
they found in plant foods.

00:11:57.440 --> 00:12:01.200
And unfortunately, cooking doesn’t
destroy pollutants like DDE—

00:12:01.200 --> 00:12:04.720
in fact it may make them
even more concentrated.

00:12:04.720 --> 00:12:07.280
And this is for a pesticide
that may increase the risk

00:12:07.280 --> 00:12:09.680
of Alzheimer’s disease as
much as if you carried

00:12:09.680 --> 00:12:14.720
the so-called Alzheimer’s
gene APOE&nbsp;&nbsp;4.

